Feature: Correct Nx cache contracts
  Scenario: Side effects always execute
    Given a setup or publish target inherits a cacheable default
    When Nx resolves the project
    Then the target is uncached

  Scenario: Continuous tasks own a live process
    Given a development or watch target
    When Nx resolves the project
    Then the target is continuous and uncached

  Scenario: Native source dependencies invalidate consumers
    Given two Cargo packages linked by a path dependency
    When the dependency changes
    Then Nx records the consumer edge with manifest provenance
    And a frontend without that dependency stays unaffected

  Scenario: A cache restores only owned deliverables
    Given a target with an explicit deliverable directory
    When the deliverables are deleted after a successful run
    Then the second run restores identical bytes and executable permissions
    And a consumer executes the restored artifact

  Scenario: Invalid project metadata is visible
    Given two metadata files declare the same project name
    When Nx discovers the graph
    Then graph construction fails with both paths

  Scenario: Build inputs exclude test-only changes
    Given a source file and a test fixture
    When only the test fixture changes
    Then the production build remains cached
    And its test result is invalidated

  Scenario: Generator output authority supplies restorable Nx deliverables
    Given the schema-owned generator contracts
    When Nx resolves a deterministic generator
    Then its complete output roots are cacheable artifacts
    And every declared source pattern affects its hash
    And registry catalog membership affects its hash
    And freshness checks inspect the current generated bytes

  Scenario: Invalid dynamic inputs prevent cached restoration
    Given a cached generator result with a required uncached validation task
    When its current dynamic input validation fails
    Then Nx fails the task graph before restoring the cached result

  Scenario: Setup resolves only current native projects
    Given the bootstrap contract names the current .NET support library and Python environments
    When Nx resolves setup and the styling consumer
    Then restore belongs to the .NET project and its build owns only staged deliverables
    And Python workspace membership contains no removed projects
    And styling generation has one writer
    And CMake configuration contains no removed application or implicit dependency installation

  Scenario: Public commands execute one script and expose prerequisites to Nx
    Given the entrypoint contract selects coordinator startup and logo export
    When Nx resolves their targets
    Then each target invokes exactly one repository script
    And the producer appears in dependsOn before the consumer runs

  Scenario: Stopping the public Nx wrapper terminates its development task
    Given the coordinator has become healthy through the public Nx entrypoint
    When the wrapper receives the cancellation signal
    Then Nx and its executable stop within the shutdown deadline
    And the health endpoint no longer accepts connections
